WEBVTT

1
00:00:54.083 --> 00:00:59.208
<b>In previous verses, Krishna shed </b>
<b>deep light on sacrifices,</b>

2
00:00:59.208 --> 00:01:03.416
<b>and continuing this topic, </b>
<b>in the twenty-eighth verse,</b>

3
00:01:03.416 --> 00:01:07.041
<b>Krishna describes four more types of sacrifices,</b>

4
00:01:07.041 --> 00:01:11.250
<b>followed by a discussion of yoga </b>
<b>in the twenty-ninth verse.</b>

5
00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:18.083
<b>Here, He will speak of pranayama, which </b>
<b>is a part of the eight-limbed yoga path.</b>

6
00:01:22.875 --> 00:01:24.500
<b>In the twenty-eighth verse,</b>

7
00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:29.291
<b>Lord Krishna describes that those walking the </b>
<b>path of spiritual practice</b>

8
00:01:29.291 --> 00:01:32.583
<b>perform four types of sacrifices.</b>

9
00:01:32.583 --> 00:01:35.541
<b>While these sacrifices differ in form,</b>

10
00:01:35.541 --> 00:01:38.375
<b>but they share the same purpose:</b>

11
00:01:38.375 --> 00:01:42.041
<b>purification of mind and spiritual advancement.</b>

12
00:01:42.041 --> 00:01:47.750
<b>Some engage in material sacrifice, which</b>
<b>is the offering of wealth or possessions.</b>

13
00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:50.708
<b>This can be done through charity,</b>

14
00:01:50.708 --> 00:01:56.958
<b>where people dedicate their </b>
<b>resources to help others.</b>

15
00:01:56.958 --> 00:02:00.458
<b>By sharing wealth and possessions with others,</b>

16
00:02:00.458 --> 00:02:07.541
<b>one's attachment to worldly things</b>
<b>diminishes and the mind becomes pure.</b>

17
00:02:07.541 --> 00:02:08.458
<b>Think</b>

18
00:02:08.458 --> 00:02:11.708
<b>of it as breaking free from bondage,</b>

19
00:02:11.708 --> 00:02:17.583
<b>where you willingly break the </b>
<b>chains of wealth and property</b>

20
00:02:17.583 --> 00:02:22.166
<b>The second is the sacrifice of austerity, </b>
<b>a form of spiritual discipline.</b>

21
00:02:22.166 --> 00:02:28.500
<b>This includes strict self-discipline, such </b>
<b>as fasting or renouncing certain things,</b>

22
00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:32.166
<b>following specific rules and practices.</b>

23
00:02:32.166 --> 00:02:40.375
<b>Its purpose is to purify body and mind, </b>
<b>allowing focus on spiritual needs.</b>

24
00:02:40.375 --> 00:02:44.958
<b>Then there's the sacrifice of yoga, which</b>
<b>is the practice of eight-limbed yoga.</b>

25
00:02:44.958 --> 00:02:52.500
<b>This involves breath control, physical postures, </b>
<b>meditation, and other techniques</b>

26
00:02:52.500 --> 00:03:00.041
<b>that prove invaluable in gaining mastery over </b>
<b>mind and body, leading to self-realization.</b>

27
00:03:00.041 --> 00:03:04.000
<b>The fourth sacrifice is the sacrifice of </b>
<b>knowledge through self-study,</b>

28
00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:09.416
<b>which is the path of attaining supreme </b>
<b>wisdom through studying sacred texts.</b>

29
00:03:09.416 --> 00:03:15.708
<b>Here, instead of sensual pleasures, one </b>
<b>dedicates their time and intellect to study.</b>

30
00:03:15.708 --> 00:03:22.708
<b>In essence, it's an offering of time and </b>
<b>intelligence for spiritual growth.</b>

31
00:03:22.708 --> 00:03:31.458
<b>Krishna's message is that all these forms of </b>
<b>sacrifice aid in humanity's spiritual progress.</b>

32
00:03:31.458 --> 00:03:36.708
<b>Following this, in the twenty-ninth verse, </b>
<b>Krishna mentions another sacrifice</b>

33
00:03:36.708 --> 00:03:39.125
<b>related to pranayama.</b>

34
00:03:39.125 --> 00:03:41.625
<b>Those who practice this sacrifice or discipline</b>

35
00:03:41.625 --> 00:03:47.041
<b>control their life force, which means</b>
<b>breath, entering their body.</b>

36
00:03:47.041 --> 00:03:54.791
<b>This involves various techniques of </b>
<b>inhaling, holding, and exhaling breath,</b>

37
00:03:54.791 --> 00:03:58.916
<b>which helps in achieving physical </b>
<b>and mental stability.</b>

38
00:03:58.916 --> 00:04:03.166
<b>Some practitioners also reduce their food intake</b>

39
00:04:03.166 --> 00:04:08.625
<b>and control their senses</b>
<b>through dietary discipline.</b>

40
00:04:08.625 --> 00:04:14.583
<b>This aids not only in physical stability </b>
<b>but also in spiritual advancement.</b>

41
00:04:14.583 --> 00:04:15.666
<b>And finally –</b>

42
00:04:15.666 --> 00:04:18.458
<b>two points are essential to remember:</b>

43
00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:22.791
<b>First - that while walking the path of self-control,</b>

44
00:04:22.791 --> 00:04:30.333
<b>the sacrifice of breath, food, time, etc., is </b>
<b>equivalent to a sacred offering.</b>

45
00:04:30.333 --> 00:04:31.500
<b>Second –</b>

46
00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:37.125
<b>while the sacrifices mentioned in these</b>
<b>two verses certainly aid spiritual progress,</b>

47
00:04:37.125 --> 00:04:40.416
<b>far above all these is the path of devotion,</b>

48
00:04:40.416 --> 00:04:48.375
<b>where you surrender yourself and the results </b>
<b>of all your actions to Lord Krishna.</b>

49
00:04:48.375 --> 00:04:53.916
<b>This path provides far greater spiritual</b>
<b>advancement than these sacrifices</b>

50
00:04:53.916 --> 00:04:54.916
<b>and</b>

51
00:04:54.916 --> 00:04:57.375
<b>leads to liberation.</b>

52
00:05:02.166 --> 00:05:04.125
<b>In these verses,</b>

53
00:05:04.125 --> 00:05:07.833
<b>the focus is on the knowledge </b>
<b>sacrifice of self-study—</b>

54
00:05:07.833 --> 00:05:16.000
<b>Which means dedicating your time to the </b>
<b>study of the Vedas and scriptures.</b>

55
00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:21.166
<b>You could have spent your </b>
<b>time on many other things,</b>

56
00:05:21.166 --> 00:05:29.083
<b>such as entertainment, foods and drinks, </b>
<b>sleep, or some other material pleasure.</b>

57
00:05:29.083 --> 00:05:37.625
<b>Yet, by taking out this time, you are </b>
<b>reading this Gita and understanding it.</b>

58
00:05:37.625 --> 00:05:47.833
<b>Regular study of the scriptures </b>
<b>guides you towards spiritual progress.</b>

59
00:05:47.833 --> 00:05:54.791
<b>Regular study of the scriptures </b>
<b>guides you towards spiritual progress.</b>

60
00:05:54.791 --> 00:05:57.083
<b>Imagine,</b>

61
00:05:57.083 --> 00:06:02.416
<b>starting each day with a verse </b>
<b>from the Bhagavad Gita.</b>

62
00:06:02.416 --> 00:06:07.500
<b>It is like meeting me daily,</b>

63
00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:18.958
<b>your friend who only and only wants </b>
<b>your spiritual growth and everyone’s well-being.</b>

64
00:06:18.958 --> 00:06:20.458
<b>But</b>

65
00:06:20.458 --> 00:06:22.166
<b>remember,</b>

66
00:06:22.166 --> 00:06:26.916
<b>this sacrifice should not be limited to study alone.</b>

67
00:06:26.916 --> 00:06:31.166
<b>It is necessary to understand these principles,</b>

68
00:06:31.166 --> 00:06:36.291
<b>take some more time to reflect on them,</b>

69
00:06:36.291 --> 00:06:44.708
<b>and think about how you can </b>
<b>apply them in your life.</b>

70
00:06:44.708 --> 00:06:47.000
<b>reflect upon this.</b>

71
00:06:51.833 --> 00:06:54.041
<b>"Yajna"</b>

72
00:06:54.041 --> 00:07:00.291
<b>this word conjures up an image in the mind—</b>

73
00:07:00.291 --> 00:07:12.166
<b>an image of a sacrificial altar, a burning fire, </b>
<b>and offerings of ghee and materials.</b>

74
00:07:12.166 --> 00:07:13.208
<b>But</b>

75
00:07:13.208 --> 00:07:15.666
<b>yajna is not just that;</b>

76
00:07:15.666 --> 00:07:25.458
<b>yajna is every sacrifice that purifies your </b>
<b>soul and contributes to human welfare.</b>

77
00:07:25.458 --> 00:07:28.958
<b>For instance, the sacrifice of wealth —</b>

78
00:07:28.958 --> 00:07:35.416
<b>sacrificing your money or </b>
<b>possessions to help others.</b>

79
00:07:35.416 --> 00:07:40.291
<b>This awakens a sense of generosity </b>
<b>and dedication in the mind.</b>

80
00:07:40.291 --> 00:07:46.166
<b>The only requirement is that while </b>
<b>making this sacrifice or donation,</b>

81
00:07:46.166 --> 00:07:52.416
<b>there should be no desire for any </b>
<b>reward or gain in your mind.</b>

82
00:07:52.416 --> 00:07:53.875
<b>Now think about</b>

83
00:07:53.875 --> 00:08:01.375
<b>how much this sacrifice gives you in a </b>
<b>family setting, even without asking.</b>

84
00:08:01.375 --> 00:08:09.791
<b>A family that regularly practices charity </b>
<b>and helps those in need —</b>

85
00:08:09.791 --> 00:08:16.458
<b>the members of that family, especially the </b>
<b>children, will learn so many essential life values.</b>

86
00:08:16.458 --> 00:08:18.000
<b>The value of compassion.</b>

87
00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:19.791
<b>The value of empathy.</b>

88
00:08:19.791 --> 00:08:21.583
<b>The value of assistance.</b>

89
00:08:21.583 --> 00:08:23.958
<b>The value of human welfare.</b>

90
00:08:23.958 --> 00:08:26.041
<b>Now consider</b>

91
00:08:26.041 --> 00:08:39.625
<b>how helpful family members who selflessly help </b>
<b>others will be to each other in times of distress.</b>

92
00:08:39.625 --> 00:08:42.333
<b>How valuable is this lesson?</b>

93
00:08:42.333 --> 00:08:46.333
<b>And that is the beauty of yajna.</b>

94
00:08:46.333 --> 00:08:56.208
<b>The more you dedicate, the more value </b>
<b>automatically arises in your life.</b>

95
00:09:01.041 --> 00:09:05.416
<b>The question must have arisen in your mind:</b>

96
00:09:05.416 --> 00:09:12.000
<b>how can yajna be incorporated </b>
<b>into professional life?</b>

97
00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.375
<b>It certainly can be.</b>

98
00:09:14.375 --> 00:09:17.666
<b>Take the example of the sacrifice of wealth —</b>

99
00:09:17.666 --> 00:09:22.791
<b>sacrificing your money or </b>
<b>possessions to help others.</b>

100
00:09:22.791 --> 00:09:28.666
<b>Selflessly dedicating something </b>
<b>valuable to others.</b>

101
00:09:28.666 --> 00:09:33.750
<b>You also have professional </b>
<b>knowledge and experience.</b>

102
00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:36.791
<b>This, too, is extremely valuable,</b>

103
00:09:36.791 --> 00:09:46.250
<b>and when you dedicate it selflessly to others, </b>
<b>this dedication takes the form of a yajna.</b>

104
00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:52.875
<b>Moreover, the sacrifice of austerity also </b>
<b>has its importance in professional life,</b>

105
00:09:52.875 --> 00:09:57.500
<b>expressed in the form of </b>
<b>hard work and dedication.</b>

106
00:09:57.500 --> 00:10:03.916
<b>Just as a yogi performs austerities </b>
<b>for their inner purification,</b>

107
00:10:03.916 --> 00:10:04.916
<b>similarly,</b>

108
00:10:04.916 --> 00:10:09.333
<b>an employee remains dedicated to their work,</b>

109
00:10:09.333 --> 00:10:13.750
<b>simplifying the lives of </b>
<b>customers through that work.</b>

110
00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:16.708
<b>The only important thing is that</b>

111
00:10:16.708 --> 00:10:23.500
<b>there should be a spirit of dedication and </b>
<b>cooperation for others in it,</b>

112
00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:27.291
<b>not material or economic gain.</b>

113
00:10:27.291 --> 00:10:31.625
<b>Don't hoard your experiences; share them.</b>

114
00:10:31.625 --> 00:10:36.541
<b>Do every professional task with a spirit of service.</b>

115
00:10:36.541 --> 00:10:41.166
<b>By doing so, you too will partake in the yajna.</b>

116
00:10:41.166 --> 00:10:44.958
<b>Such people not only achieve personal success</b>

117
00:10:44.958 --> 00:10:49.833
<b>but also set an example and inspire others,</b>

118
00:10:49.833 --> 00:10:55.500
<b>and through this, the level of </b>
<b>the entire organization rises.</b>

119
00:10:55.500 --> 00:11:02.000
<b>Yajna is both possible and </b>
<b>necessary in professional life.</b>

